    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="gt_d43">

                <pb facs="gt_d43-1" n="1" xml:id="gt_d43-1"/>

                <head>GT–43. Telegram from the Secretary of State to the Embassy in Guatemala<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="gt_d43-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Guatemala City</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-11-18T23:24:00-06:00">November 18, 1960,
                            11:24 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>350. Ten million dollars approved by Under Secretary Dillon for imports from the
                    U.S. with counterpart being granted to the GOG as accrued. Detailed information
                    to follow. You may wish convey info President Ydígoras.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="gt_d43-f2"/> Public announcement left to your and President’s <pb
                        facs="0820" n="732" type="typeset" xml:id="pg732"/> discretion. If public
                    announcement contemplated, please give department 24 hours advance notice to
                    permit consideration simultaneous release Washington.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="gt_d43-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#gt_d43-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="gt_d43-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 814.10/11–1860. Confidential;
                    Priority. Drafted by Carwell and signed by Higdon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#gt_d43-f2" n="2" xml:id="gt_d43-f2-content">
                <p>Muccio informed Ydígoras and Unda Murillo on November 19. (Telegram 260 from
                    Guatemala City, November 23, 1960; 814.10/11–2360)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#gt_d43-f3" n="3" xml:id="gt_d43-f3-content">
                <p>Ydígoras and Muccio agreed on an announcement to be issued to the press on
                    December 10. It referred to agreement on a $9.6 million loan for the Rio Hondo
                    road and the El Molino highway, and approved of a $10 million grant to assist
                    the Guatemalan Government. (Telegram 284 from Guatemala City, December 8, 1960;
                    714.5–MSP/12–860) No record of a simultaneous release in Washington was
                    found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
